/E (Flowcharts are useful because they provide a clear visual overview of how an algorithm works. By showing each step in a diagram, it becomes easier to spot errors, unnecessary loops, or missing processes. Flowcharts are also helpful when explaining logic to people who may not understand programming, as the visuals make the sequence of actions easy to follow. In addition, they play an important role in system design and documentation by offering a simple and organized representation of the workflow.)
